@display("Delivery")
delivery: section {
  | How a product gets built is the implementation's: its project, with `std/project`, holds
  | the components its code is divided into and the plan of the work. A story is a change to the
  | spec, a list of the items it adds or changes; it owns no behaviour of its own, so the spec
  | stays the one statement of what the product does, and a delivered story can be thrown away.
  |
  | | Kind                          | Holds                                                                   |
  | | ----------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |
  | | `component(path, …, lang)`    | `uses`, responsibilities and `exports`, its references naming the parts it builds |
  | | `story(refs…, adds, changes)` | the goals it advances, the spec items it adds and changes, and its `done` |
  | | `increment(delivers)`         | the stories a shippable slice delivers, and its `done`                  |
  | | `milestone(reached_by)`       | what a point in time is measured against, and its `done`                |
  | | `done`                        | the delivery-only items the work is accepted by, as prose               |

  component_kind: term {{
    `name: component("internal/parser", parser, lang = "go") { … }`, a unit of the
    implementation's code with one contract, at a path from the repository's root. Its
    references after the path name the spec's parts, actors or sections it builds, `uses` lists
    the components it may import, and an `exports` holds part of its exported interface
    verbatim. It's architecture, never a spec kind.
  }}

  story_kind: term {{
    `name: story(goal, adds = [items], changes = [items]) { … }`, one change to the spec, small
    enough to build in one `increment`: the goals and qualities its references name, the
    requirements it adds and changes, and a `done` for what delivery alone needs. It's accepted when the items it
    lists are proven at their current [revisions](#heron.language.specifications.layers.revisions.revision).
  }}

  delivery_kinds_in_project: rule(system.checker) {
    must {{ declare `component`, `story`, `increment`, `milestone`, `done` and the delivery flags in `std/project`, with no [layer](#heron.language.specifications.layers.layer) }}
  }

  story_lists_items: rule(system.checker) {
    if {{ a story holds a `given`, a `when`, a `then` or a strength node }}
    must {{ report it as an error at the node: a story lists spec items and states no behaviour }}
  }

  story_accepted: rule(system.interpreter) {
    must {{ count a story as accepted when every item it adds or changes is proven at its current [revision](#heron.language.specifications.layers.revisions.revision), and list the rest under it in the conformance report }}
  }

  story_view: rule(system.docs_generator) {
    must {{ show a story with the goal it advances and the items it adds and changes, each linked and with its proof status, then its `done` }}
  }

  one_status_each: rule(system.linter) {
    if {{ a node carries two flags of the group `"status"` }}
    must {{ report the second as an error of the flag's group }}
  }

  component_view: rule(system.docs_generator) {
    must {{ show a component with its path, the parts it implements, the components it uses and those that use it under "Used by", and its exports }}
  }

  uses_enforced: rule(system.linter) {
    if {{ a component's code imports a component its `uses` doesn't list }}
    should {{ report it as a warning at the component }}
  }

  errors: section {
    @display("Behaviour in a story")
    behaviour_in_story: error("story") {
      title = "story {story} holds a {kind}; a story lists the spec items it adds or changes, which state the behaviour"
      story: field(String)
      kind: field(String)
      | Reported as [story_lists_items] says.
    }

    @display("Import outside uses")
    @severity(warning)
    import_outside_uses: error("component-uses") {
      title = "{component} imports {other}, which its uses doesn't list"
      component: field(String)
      other: field(String)
      | An import that breaks a component's contract.
      | Reported as [uses_enforced] says.
    }
  }

  @display("A story in a project")
  delivery_example: example {
    | ```heron
    | import = ["std/doc@1", "std/project@1"]
    |
    | self_service: goal {{ Customers fix a wrong charge themselves. }}
    |
    | late_rejected: rule {
    |   must {{ reject a refund after the window }}
    | }
    |
    | refund_window: story(self_service, adds = [late_rejected]) {
    |   done {{ The support team has seen the new message. }}
    | }
    |
    | first: increment(refund_window) {{ Refunds without a ticket. }}
    | ```
  }
}
